{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here","id":317752,"title":"Promethean and Transhumanism Goes Here","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-20T16:18:38-08:00","id":317752,"title":"Promethean and Transhumanism Goes Here","content":"The intersection of these spheres is a great source of great argument, but it can derail other threads. Why not bring it in here?<br /> <br /> Let's start: Centimani is the transhumanist &quot;Refinement&quot;, as it pushes the Promethean outside of human norms of being, thinking, and moralizing. Or, Centimani is <i>not </i>a transhumanist &quot;Refinement&quot; because it is in fact neutral to the borders of human experience, and further dwells on the current misery of the Saturnine Night without a means of ending it. Or, ... .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T20:15:03-08:00","id":317887,"title":"","content":"You can (if you wanted to) actually view Promethean as a humanist metaphor for transhumanism for whatever it's worth. The characters are changing themselves to overcome the limitations of their condition. It's just that they're starting &quot;below&quot; humanity - but the direction being strived in is still the same.<br /> <br /> I don't believe the Centimani can be viewed as transhumanist because &quot;human&quot; doesn't lie anywhere on their continuum. You can't transition from or through something you've never been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T21:09:43-08:00","id":317933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=317887#post317887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe the Centimani can be viewed as transhumanist because &quot;human&quot; doesn't lie anywhere on their continuum. You can't transition from or through something you've never been.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can, just like I pointed before - in posthuman state, Uplifted dolphines or chimpanzee weren't never humans. But still they will be posthumanity, joining the new kind of humanity with they thoughs or personas.<br /> <br /> The problem with Centimani is that isn't looking for transhumanity in itself - <b>maybe</b> a posthumanity, but in my eyes, most of it is &quot;I need any possible power, and will destroy universe to get it&quot;. They seed Flux, unmaking the reality itself, just to get an edge on those around you. It's not transhumanity, it's <b>anti</b>-humanity, like it was stated in their post topic.<br /> <br /> The true transhuman Refinements are probably Argentum, Ferrum and Plumbum. First is analyzing those that suppress humans in some way ( other supernaturals of WoD ). Second is about physical and mental might, naturally leading to evolution of this particular specimen of Created. Last one is not looking on humanity as particular template, but on Created themselves, wanting to analyze their of kind - and maybe fixing they own &quot;curses&quot;, like Torment, or Disfigurments.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem the transhumanistic Created would have is the need to end they Pilgrimage as humanity - even if, in some way, New Adam is better than humans. The main problem of them is that they have those &quot;curses&quot; that are problems, not they supernatural strengths or long lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T03:49:41-08:00","id":318148,"title":"","content":"If a Promethean was transhumanist, I think he should just try to become a better human and that way try to surpass the human limits. At least in the first edition, redeemed Prometheans kept all skills and attributes above 5, which is technically transhuman. Furthermore, Athanors also resulted in possibly transhuman abilities.<br /> <br /> In Promethean it is not possible to fully surpass the human condition, but you can always try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T10:02:37-08:00","id":318322,"title":"","content":"I agree with the notion that 'transhumanist' requires humanity as a base, and that the Created \u2013 as not-yet human \u2013 ought to be, <i>ipso facto</i>, unable to attain such a state. However, IF a Centimanus could use any of the arts associated with Flux on a human, that COULD allow for some form of transhumanist exploration. In First Edition, all of the Pandoran Transmutations are exclusively directed at the user's own body, but we don't yet know what sorts of things Second Edition Freaks might be capable of doing.<br /> <br /> As for an exemplary transhumanist Refinement, I'd offer that Argentum comes closest, as it seeks to understand those things that were once human (or still human, in the case of mages), and the seeking of how one can move beyond the proper human state is \u2013 in a highly didactic view of etymology \u2013 the very definition of 'transhuman' state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T10:41:37-08:00","id":318357,"title":"","content":"I never got the feeling that people were looking for specifically transhumanism from promethean so much as....inhumanism? Nonhumanism? Parahumanism?<br /> <br /> Basically, the idea of this universal principle that privileges humanity specifically as the paragon of everything a thinking being should aspire to be strikes some folks as off, me included. I'll give that there are some things about humans that are neat, but there's nothing specifically about a human meatcase, or a precisely human psychology, that is necessary for those things.<br /> <br /> Like, what I would ideally want, especially for the unfleshed, is not necessarily &quot;I have achieved humanity and surpassed it&quot;, but rather &quot;I have become complete, but not human. I am something else&quot; as a possible endpoint. The idea of robots transmogrifying magically into a particularly smart ape at the end of their pilgrimage just seems weird the longer I think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T19:01:32-08:00","id":318633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=318357#post318357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of robots transmogrifying magically into a particularly smart ape at the end of their pilgrimage just seems weird the longer I think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking of humans as &quot;particularly smart apes&quot; is obviously not helping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T20:22:14-08:00","id":318653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=318357#post318357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, the idea of this universal principle that privileges humanity specifically as the paragon of everything a thinking being should aspire to be strikes some folks as off, me included. I'll give that there are some things about humans that are neat, but there's nothing specifically about a human meatcase, or a precisely human psychology, that is necessary for those things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, in the nWOD, it may just be. Certainly anything that doesn't have a human base has an abnormally high chance of being evil or just often do evil. And those who are good(such as Prometheans or the Unchained) either seeks to be human or have incorporated human aspects into themselves(respectively).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T23:22:41-08:00","id":318771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=317933#post317933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can, just like I pointed before - in posthuman state, Uplifted dolphines or chimpanzee weren't never humans. But still they will be posthumanity, joining the new kind of humanity with they thoughs or personas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since you obviously missed my post addressing your misunderstanding/mudding of transhumanism in the other thread. So here it is again:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Um...no. The idea of &quot;uplifting&quot; less developed species is a sci-fi trapping that ties into the idea of culture/technology progression an organisms development beyond its normal biological abilities (which is very similar to the transhuman ideal but not actually the same thing). Dolphins made super intelligent by cybernetics or gene-manipulation or whatever are &quot;transpersons/transdolphines&quot; not &quot;transhumans&quot;. Your mixing up the concept of &quot;person hood&quot; with humanity, the two are separate.<br /> <br /> So to provide the definition of transhumanism:<br /> <br /> <i>Noun</i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i> - the belief or theory that the </i></span><b>human race</b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i> can evolve beyond its current physical and mental limitations, especially </i></span><b>by means of science and technology</b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i>.</i></span><br /> <br /> So, as mentioned here, for one to be transhuman, one would first need to be human. Something Prometheans are not. </div> </div> </div>Uplifted animals would/could never &quot;join&quot; the human race. Because they are not biologically the same species as us. Even in a transhuman context where a human has heightened mental acuity due the same process/mechanism that uplifted another animal the two would still be distinct species. That's how biological distinction via species stratification works. One could argue them as a new genus/sub-genus of their respective species, but the fact they have both become &quot;super intelligent&quot; does not automatically enter them into the same species. <br /> <br /> Uplifted animals could engage with a human/transhuman as other PEOPLE or sentient beings of potential intellect, they could likely contribute to a transhuman society, but they themselves would not be transhuman. As I mentioned before, your mixing up biological and social constructs here and expanding the term transhuman beyond its actual definition quite a bit. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=318633#post318633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking of humans as &quot;particularly smart apes&quot; is obviously not helping.</div> </div> </div> </div>Satchel, don't waste your time man. This thread might as well be titled &quot;Promethean and Missing the Point&quot;. People who engage in the transhuman ideal inherently have issue with the state of humanity and are going to devalue it. <br /> <br /> In real life I'm all for transhumanism and I think most people are at least intellecutally aware of the flaws present in human society, biology and psychology. Being from a social science background I'm a little more skeptical then most about the practical distribution of transhumanism in a human society. I'm also pretty aware that in some ways humanity and being human is pretty awesome as is and that people can be capable of amazing things despite their &quot;limitations&quot;. <br /> <br /> However, in the case of NWoD and in particular Promethean I agree that humanity should be represented as &quot;special&quot; in some way. <br /> <br /> In the metaphysics of most NWoD game lines we have souls, no reflection in the shadow, leave ghosts, are the favoured tools of the God-Machine, are the only creatures able to Awaken, the only meat things worth dragging back to Arcadia, are the base from which (and may be required) all save one major supernatural (Demons) springs from. That starts to sound like a laundry list of things that the supernatural world seems to think we are pretty unique and special in regards to. <br /> <br /> Add to this the fact that pretty much every attempt in the NWoD to go &quot;transhuman&quot; is pretty much evil (yes their are exceptions, but they are exactly that, rare instances not involved with antithical amoral means/methods/aims) e.g. Mage Litches, Modified Chieron Hunters, all Mummy's, two of the three major types of immortals, the majority of Archmages ect. Hell even the majority of post-human states are pretty suckie really - Vamparism, Werewolfism, Changelinghood and Geistism. All have pretty hefty innate drawback (see Vamparism) or throw you into inhuman methods of thought (from a human perspective) and engage with inhuman societies that do break you down to a certain extent and give you an imperative that throws you in dangers way (Werewolf is perhaps the best example, Geist and Changeling both have elements of this as well though). <br /> <br /> Really, the only &quot;transhumans&quot; that don't get an utterly obvious drawback innately or through their social structures is Mages. Even then, being a Mage is what you make of it and is very much fraught with falls to hubris, madness, corruption (both moral and spiritual) and exposes one to a tone of supernatural threats. <br /> <br /> This is not to say that transhumanism should always be view as negative within the context of every game line in the NWoD. I'm happy having the Ordo Dracul and its &quot;transvampirism&quot; being portrayed as a good thing. Mage should engage with transhumanism as a sub-genre of its theme of hubris and wisdom. Hunter (at least a tier 3 game) should engage with at what point a &quot;transhuman&quot; hunter is just another inhuman monster. Demon should engage with the uniqueness of humanity as a contrast to the uniqueness of the Unchained and the &quot;transdemonic&quot; state that Hell may represent is an obvious parallel.<br /> <br /> My point is more that devaluing humanity (not human life, that something that should be devalued in inhuman/supernatural horror games I feel, particularly by morally dubious characters) I feel takes away from the NWoD in some ways. Yes you can use it to great effect if you want to run some sort of existential horror element in a Lovecraftian vain about the universe not giving a shit about humanity. That's a particular type of game and it has its place in the NWoD rosta without doubt, I just don't think its the baseline assumption of the majority of the gamelines.<br /> <br /> All this being said, the golden rules applies. If you want humanity to be nothing special and the aim of transcending the species norm to be the &quot;big good&quot; ideal of the setting in your games go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T23:47:25-08:00","id":318778,"title":"","content":"Something that I feel is of minor relevance to what Hawthorn said is a little fact strung throughout the games, though most strongly in Mage, Hunter, and Beast(So far), is a re-emphasis on how humanity is kind of the source. In truth, you have to go far afield within the text to some pretty minor stuff to find something that doesn't even suggest humanity behind. Even things like the Abyss and the God Machine have subtle subtextual indications that the whole World of Darkness comes back to humanity and it's fears, with the context that humanity has all the power to banish it back as much as summon it up.<br /> <br /> Humanity is the pure state, it is a prima materia for reality itself in a way. It is not glorious, it is not beautiful, and it's not exalted per se, and yet by virtues as the origin point it is, in a way, the highest form of life within humanity. A human has the freedom to suffer any incarnation of power that comes it's way, a freedom sorely lacked by anything else, <i>particularly</i> Prometheans.<br /> <br /> Or, put another way, &quot;They told me I could become anything, so I did&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T01:09:37-08:00","id":318790,"title":"","content":"I agree with <b>Hawthorn</b> as to that games are written as humanity-centric ( I'm not blind to context guys, really ). I also read some idea - I don't remember what was the user name of this - that run &quot;cosmic&quot; <b>Mage</b> with alien races in Milky Way Galaxy. And they <b>all</b> have Supernal Souls.<br /> <br /> I like to think the cosmology of WoD as this - humans are special, because we are telling stories on Earth. If we would tell them on other planets, they would be about other intelligent lifeforms. <b>With</b> souls. Probably.<br /> <br /> As <b>Hawthorn</b> pointed also, in setting there is place for Lovecraftian bit &quot;humanity isn't special species&quot;. I would rather coined it in to &quot;humanity isn't only special species&quot;. Yes, game lines favor humans as they are written from they perspective. And they have most sense in point of looking from the Earth. But it's not the only answer.<br /> <br /> Also, I advise on looking at <a href=\"http://www.buzzfeed.com/daves4/the-universe-is-scary\" target=\"_blank\">those few pictures</a>, to really get the understand position of humanity in the cosmos. Just for the enlightenment on your life. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Back to the Promethean and transhumanism topic - I don't think that transhuman Created are popular, in great numbers. Or that they truly <b>are right</b>. They are just giving other answer to the question &quot;What should I do with mine existence?&quot; compared to classical seeking New Dawn Prometheans. I think they object in the game will only add to the setting - they are those that don't agree with typical PCs and <b>neither</b> of sides can't tell they are absolute right. Redemption seeking Prometheans will argue that universe favors them - and even Principle is supporting they quest. &quot;Transhuman&quot; Created will point that New Dawn is taking it's toll on you, and you giving up powers and knowledge you were collecting in previous life. Why would you need this if this should be Prize, after all years of Pilgrimage?<br /> <br /> Both sides are correct, and it's only to players and their characters to decide. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T09:02:07-08:00","id":318985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=318778#post318778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, put another way, &quot;They told me I could become anything, so I did&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something that I've been wrestling with the phrasing of lately amounts to hitching together things like Zo Malak's musings on bans, the way the Arisen's Descent counter works once they've completed their allotted task, and the brief moment of non-being experienced by a Falling angel \u2014 the supernatural denizens of the World of Darkness, generally speaking, have to justify their existence/presence in it; of the things that don't have to do likewise, humans (whether by delicate balance of or complete lack of innate purposes) are among the few who aren't inanimate or nonsapient.<br /> <br /> The Promethean purpose is to transcend the need for purpose. Humans exist for the sake of existing, and that's the goddamn golden ticket of ontological comfortability, broadly speaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T09:12:10-08:00","id":318990,"title":"","content":"(*is writing to this to Je N'ai Pas De Mots, so you can suffer mood whiplash as I have*)<br /> <br /> Another point occurs to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game is explicitly anti-transhumanist, in that it's always shown to cost more than it's worth; sorry if that upsets you, but we're making a horror game here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forget transhumanism and post humanism and humanism. Let's remember <i>this is a horror game</i>.<br /> <br /> Explictly, this is a game whose thesis statement says the horror comes from discovering that the world is filled with nightmares, and now that you know you can't go back. That implies in certain ways that advancement is inherently terrifying <i>first</i>, with a fear of stagnation being addressed but treated as <i>second. </i>The sort of advancements that make modern transhumanism possible stem from technological and societal changes that have only pushed humanity deeper into their comforting lie that the monsters don't exist, exaggerating the problem.<br /> <br /> In plainer terms, this is a game whose opening line says you were better for having not checked the noises in the alley or the colors under the bed. This isn't a fault of the game, it's a fault of the genre, and if that's part of what the genre does, the evocation of fear in the things we all have in common, I'm not sure you can call it a fault. Yes, the game(and genre) acknowledges that staying put isn't better, that things still happen in ignorance, but that comes after &quot;The most horrible thing to happen to you is that you moved away from the familiar and the comfortable enough to find out disturbing secrets&quot;. And that's always a choice, by the way, a character can work to convince themselves to ignore even instances that are shoved on them(the movie Oculus has a great example of this, by the way).<br /> <br /> Prometheans are unique in that they are born under the bed, but have the instincts to hide under the sheets. They can do what every other protagonist in the World, subtextually, wishes they could do-they <i>can </i>go back under the sheets. It's a terrible notion for progress, but again, that's the genre. It pits the ideas of a person going forth and hiding together in the Pilgramage, the character can learn and discover about humanity and earn the right to forget the most horrific aspect of the World, to assume step zero.<br /> <br /> That grates against players, I know. It grates against me! I don't play the WoD as a horror game, I do it as a dark urban fantasy. As much as I like my external nightmares and personal horror and tragedy and such, in the end I like triumphant victories, self-actualization and growth in general, and endings that ultimately make the world a little brighter. Of course, I'm also way more of a humanist than I am of a transhumanist (I do believe you can be varying shades of both, and even be both of even more contradictory things), so the Pilgrimage still appeals to me on that front. But even if I use horror to inform but ultimately still not direct my use of the setting, I'm still side stepping and manipulating the basic fact-<i>this is a horror game and with that comes a certain set of standards that affect the genre</i>.<br /> <br /> Think on any horror movie or story. Think critically about it, long and deep. Then think about Promethean.<br /> <br /> Are you really surprised at what the horror genre has to say about transhumanism? Welcome to [part of] the buy in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-25-2015, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T09:23:16-08:00","id":318995,"title":"","content":"And if Promethean was written in context of that interstellar game, then they would probably have an endpoint as any of those species.<br /> <br /> However, since Promethean is, by default, set on Earth... and, well, there's only one type of critter with Integrity around here.<br /> <br /> Actually, that might be something to point out: humans (and their derivatives) are the only beings with an 'internalized' Integrity stat. Spirits? Nope. Angels? Nope. Demons? Nope (Cover is <i>entirely</i> external to the Demon. If the God-Machine wasn't out to get them, they could walk around without any Covers at all, and would be <i>perfectly OK</i>). Animals? Nope.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Also... nice link. Shame it isn't relevant to the discussion, tho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 11-22-2014, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T10:26:36-08:00","id":319049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=318790#post318790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I advise on looking at <a href=\"http://www.buzzfeed.com/daves4/the-universe-is-scary\" target=\"_blank\">those few pictures</a>, to really get the understand position of humanity in the cosmos. Just for the enlightenment on your life. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>First off, having taken a few college courses on astronomy, you haven't told me anything I don't already know.<br /> <br /> Second, it's a matter of perspective. I think one that tells me to feel scared at how small I am is a poor one.<br /> <br /> Once upon a time, when I was on my religious mission, my companion once said that he liked flying because it was a reminder of how small we are, seeing all the little toy houses and little figurines scrambling over the orange peel of the earth.<br /> <br /> That's not what I saw.<br /> <br /> I saw us cover a massive distance in something that comparatively isn't that much bigger than I am. And while riding that thing, I never once saw a place that humanity didn't touch. I saw roads, farms, tilling, observation outposts-that great distance we spanned, and humanity would never let me forget it was there.<br /> <br /> You want to try and tell me we're so small and insignificant in the vast scheme of things? Bullshit. Tell me what the universe has done aside from existing. It's big, but it's dead, it's empty, and it doesn't do shit. Sure, one day humanity will dry up, all our marks will fade, but by that time, I won't care either, so why care now. In the mean time, we're alive, and we're doing things. There's nothing else in this big, dumb, empty universe that even dares to try to live.<br /> <br /> You see ants. I see giants. You see a vast emptiness. I see a canvas waiting to be painted.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, one should not try to use the argument of &quot;But look how small we are!&quot; to someone who really fucking loves Mouse Guard.<br /> <br /> Third, not really relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T10:58:32-08:00","id":319073,"title":"","content":"The fact that humanity is the basis for so many things in the WoD makes perfect sense, being as they're some of the only sentient things on the planet, which is why the obligate focus on humanity doesn't really strain my suspension of disbelief in other lines.<br /> <br /> Promethean starts with something that is a *person* but isn't a *human*, which makes it nearly unique (until demon came along), and then posits that well, of course, the best thing they could do would be to turn into us.<br /> <br /> Which is a sentence that leaves me scratching my head. It's such a bizarre and arrogant assumption. It hits me the same as white people rolling up on a foreign shore and saying &quot;these poor people, they haven't even got a fiat economy or organized religion, how willl they ever be happy unless they become like us?&quot;<br /> <br /> And I mean, the standard argument is &quot;well, that's part of the buy-in&quot; which is why, the first time I brought this up, it was in the context of shrugging and rejecting the buy-in. This time, I'm just popping up to say there's nothing particularly transhuman about that, transhumanism is something else that involves humans transcending the limits of humanity. This would just be...things that were never human, deciding that it's possible to be a fully realized person without being human. And trying to find that sense of fulfillment and identity in a world that actively and violently rejects all other ways of being.<br /> <br /> I think that could be a good story, but it's not particularly transhuman, it's just also not one the line creators are interested in telling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T10:59:35-08:00","id":319074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=319049#post319049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, having taken a few college courses on astronomy, you haven't told me anything I don't already know.<br /> <br /> Second, it's a matter of perspective. I think one that tells me to feel scared at how small I am is a poor one.<br /> <br /> Once upon a time, when I was on my religious mission, my companion once said that he liked flying because it was a reminder of how small we are, seeing all the little toy houses and little figurines scrambling over the orange peel of the earth.<br /> <br /> That's not what I saw.<br /> <br /> I saw us cover a massive distance in something that comparatively isn't that much bigger than I am. And while riding that thing, I never once saw a place that humanity didn't touch. I saw roads, farms, tilling, observation outposts-that great distance we spanned, and humanity would never let me forget it was there.<br /> <br /> You want to try and tell me we're so small and insignificant in the vast scheme of things? Bullshit. Tell me what the universe has done aside from existing. It's big, but it's dead, it's empty, and it doesn't do shit. Sure, one day humanity will dry up, all our marks will fade, but by that time, I won't care either, so why care now. In the mean time, we're alive, and we're doing things. There's nothing else in this big, dumb, empty universe that even dares to try to live.<br /> <br /> You see ants. I see giants. You see a vast emptiness. I see a canvas waiting to be painted.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, one should not try to use the argument of &quot;But look how small we are!&quot; to someone who really fucking loves Mouse Guard.<br /> <br /> Third, not really relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arc that was beautiful and used Doctor Who references to great effect....<u><b>marry me</b></u>!<br /> <br /> Sorry that just slipped out. I'll go be quiet in this corner now.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T11:05:42-08:00","id":319088,"title":"","content":"Had I the chance, I would take you in a manly fashion. And then remember that I'm straight and feel horribly awkward about it. But still, it would be done.<br /> <br /> I actually wanted to quote the Twelfth Doctor as a third alternative, but for some reason people don't seem to like his quote about getting close to the picture rather than far away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T11:15:15-08:00","id":319092,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\">So God created man in his <i>own</i> image, in the image of God created he him; male and female created he them.</div> <br /> <br /> Sorry from bringing a little Genesis 1:26 into this, but I feel it's appropriate to the aim of the whole shebang. <hr /> <div align=\"center\">Demiurges, in playing God, create Prometheans in their own image - but, being imperfect, the likeness <i>isn't</i> complete, <i>isn't</i> perfect, <i>isn't</i> <i>done</i>.<br /> <br /> The Pilgrimage is the Promethean finishing the job, finishing <i>themselves</i>. It's beautiful and terrible and good and awful, all in one.<br /> <br /> But is it right? <i>Is it what they want</i>?<br /> <br /> Maybe. Maybe not.<br /> <br /> Change is a terrible thing. Completion is a awful thing. No one asked <i>them</i>, the half-men, the women of broken porcelain, what they wanted.<br /> <br /> &quot;But why <i>humans</i>?&quot; comes the cry. &quot;Why not something else? Some steel perfection, some beast, something new and never seen before?&quot;<br /> <br /> Because they were made to be human, for that was all their Demiurge <i>knew</i> or <i>had</i>.<br /> <br /> It's all <i>they</i> have.</div> <hr /><br /> To be less flowery for a moment, I see Prometheans in kinda the same light as I see transgender folks. They start off stuck in a body that isn't the way that it's <i>supposed</i> to be, and so they need to fix themselves.<br /> <br /> I mean, sure, a Promethean might want the ability to breath fire and fart lightning bolts, but that pales before getting a body that doesn't feel fundamentally wrong to both them and the world around them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 11-22-2014, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T11:19:13-08:00","id":319094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=319073#post319073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Promethean starts with something that is a *person* but isn't a *human*, which makes it nearly unique (until demon came along), and then posits that well, of course, the best thing they could do would be to turn into us.<br /> <br /> Which is a sentence that leaves me scratching my head. It's such a bizarre and arrogant assumption. It hits me the same as white people rolling up on a foreign shore and saying &quot;these poor people, they haven't even got a fiat economy or organized religion, how willl they ever be happy unless they become like us?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Prometheans are not foreign people and being able to live comfortably in your own mind and body is not the equivalent of a fiat economy or organized religion and <i>again</i> I must point out that looking at these things in this way is self-evidently the opposite of a useful evaluative metric.<br /> <br /> People sweeping Torment and the larger sensation it represents under the rug is not a thing I enjoy seeing treated as a legitimately informed understanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T11:58:46-08:00","id":319129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=319094#post319094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prometheans are not foreign people and being able to live comfortably in your own mind and body is not the equivalent of a fiat economy or organized religion and <i>again</i> I must point out that looking at these things in this way is self-evidently the opposite of a useful evaluative metric.</div> </div> </div> </div>Watson vs Doyle. If you accept the premise that they will necessarily be uncomfortable in their own mind and body until they become human, then yes, it all obviously follows. My problem was always with making that assumption in the first place.<br /> <br /> But the analogy to dysmorphia that I think you're implying is actually probably a big part of why this makes my personal and specific brain itch, so sure let's talk about it. I know a lot of people who are at various stages of that journey out of an uncomfortable and ill-fitting place on the gender spectrum (and, uhh...I don't like to talk about my own identity much around here, but I will count myself), many of whom have arrived (or are in the process of arriving) at some version of &quot;I will not ever fit into this structure and that is okay, I can be something else, I can be my own thing, and I can be happy and worthwhile&quot;. I probably know more people who are on a trajectory toward that particular endpoint than I do binary trans folk (ie, people who forsook one binary gender to transition into the other binary gender).<br /> <br /> So it rubs me wrong when it looks like the analogy being set up here is saying &quot;that is an, at best unfulfilling and, at worst, dangerously insane way of relating to your identity&quot;. I'm sure it's useful to someone, it just strikes really unpleasant chords with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","user":"Gabby","date":". 11-22-2014, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T12:05:43-08:00","id":319139,"title":"","content":"Arcane talking out of his ass and not completely on topic time again!<br /> <br /> You know, part of the thing that bothers me about the transhumanists having issues with a humanist game is that it seems counter-intuitive to some degrees. I mean, there are things I like about tanshumanism and find worthwhile if other problems can be worked out ahead of time, but I think there should be a core of humanism in there that needs to help guide the ethical and moral practice of transhumanism, and having issues with a game that helps foster that sense strikes me as being a little off. On a very poor comparison, it's like hiring Frank Trollman*(real name, honest, look him up) to develop the 2nd Edition of the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> *<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/holden.shearer/posts/698754346876944?comment_id=700170113402034&amp;notif_t=like\" target=\"_blank\">Holden Shearer gives a spliel of Frank's that kind of hits on what I'm getting at.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-22-2014, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T12:18:24-08:00","id":319148,"title":"","content":"I don't really think that most transhumanists (and I mean, they're welcome to crawl out of the woodwork and prove me wrong) have a problem with humanist, &quot;humanity is great (or can be great)&quot; messages. I think when they start to get antsy is when humanist works explicitly condemn or demonize transhumanism, as they are wont to do.<br /> <br /> Whether demonizing transhumanism, or a certain variety of transhumanism, is the right decision thematically is another issue. I just definitely don't think it's an issue of transhumanists looking around, going &quot;that thing has positive stuff to say about the human condition! FUCK THAT!&quot; Instead they show up when the moral shifts away from &quot;humanity is neat&quot; to &quot;trying to be immortal (or transcend some other limitation) is wrong and always ends badly, always&quot;. Assuming their issue is with the former will probably lead to you misunderstanding them most of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T12:27:12-08:00","id":319156,"title":"","content":"That just goes back to the entire &quot;What did you expect the horror genre to <i>say</i>?&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> On the entire Promethean-transhumanism argument, I'd say that the game makes a valid case for what needs to be dealt with before the achievement of transhumanism becomes a definite plus. There must be progress, but let us not be unwise in chasing it, and all that. But, again, I'm way more of a humanist than a transhumanist.<br /> <br /> But I digress. I'm not vesting too much thought into it, as it's kind of a trolly and incomplete thought anyways. I needed it out of my head though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T12:39:18-08:00","id":319184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=319156#post319156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That just goes back to the entire &quot;What did you expect the horror genre to <i>say</i>?&quot; thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never really liked this answer, and I've been trying to put my finger on why. I think it's because one of the many functions of horror is often to reinforce a societal fear, which is part of why it has become frowned upon to, for example, explicitly racially code your monsters. Using &quot;fear of other races&quot; as the currency of your horror isn't so much okay. That doesn't stop some horror movie creators from doing it anyway at various levels of subtlety, but even so.<br /> <br /> So if you ascribe to a philosophy, and horror fiction is apparently heavily invested in saying &quot;you should be scared of this&quot; every time it comes up, I can see being a bit testy about it. Especially as there are other ways to play the same situation (the horror isn't that wanting to be anything other than human is obviously and horrifically evil, the horror is that every possible escape from human frailty is booby-trapped. See: Mage)<br /> <br /> That said, for unrelated reasons I'm dizzy and have a headache, so I may not be making sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T12:51:27-08:00","id":319192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=319129#post319129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Watson vs Doyle. If you accept the premise that they will necessarily be uncomfortable in their own mind and body until they become human, then yes, it all obviously follows. My problem was always with making that assumption in the first place.<br /> <br /> But the analogy to dysmorphia that I think you're implying is actually probably a big part of why this makes my personal and specific brain itch, so sure let's talk about it. I know a lot of people who are at various stages of that journey out of an uncomfortable and ill-fitting place on the gender spectrum (and, uhh...I don't like to talk about my own identity much around here, but I will count myself), many of whom have arrived (or are in the process of arriving) at some version of &quot;I will not ever fit into this structure and that is okay, I can be something else, I can be my own thing, and I can be happy and worthwhile&quot;. I probably know more people who are on a trajectory toward that particular endpoint than I do binary trans folk (ie, people who forsook one binary gender to transition into the other binary gender).<br /> <br /> So it rubs me wrong when it looks like the analogy being set up here is saying &quot;that is an, at best unfulfilling and, at worst, dangerously insane way of relating to your identity&quot;. I'm sure it's useful to someone, it just strikes really unpleasant chords with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to apologize for any offense I might have given with my statement; I happen to be agender, and due to a sensory disorder, I am (for practical intents and purposes) incapable of being comfortable with having a body.<br /> <br /> I was making the assumption that, if you knew there was a way to make your fleshy overcoat non-hateful, you'd <i>take</i> it. I forget that most people come to terms with their discomfort and learn to cope.<br /> <br /> So it was a bad analogy. Sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T12:59:29-08:00","id":319198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=319192#post319192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would like to apologize for any offense I might have given with my statement; I happen to be agender, and due to a sensory disorder, I am (for practical intents and purposes) incapable of being comfortable with having a body.<br /> <br /> I was making the assumption that, if you knew there was a way to make your fleshy overcoat non-hateful, you'd <i>take</i> it. I forget that most people come to terms with their discomfort and learn to cope.<br /> <br /> So it was a bad analogy. Sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually somehow skipped your post entirely (for probable reasons, see: dizzy, headache). I wasn't responding to you at all, you're cool.<br /> <br /> I don't really take issue with the idea that anybody would choose the &quot;become fully comfortable&quot; option over being uncomfortable forever, I was taking issue with the fiction, on a meta level, deciding that the only way to become comfortable was by becoming this one specific thing.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the mix-up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T13:19:19-08:00","id":319263,"title":"","content":"'s OK, we're cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T13:41:44-08:00","id":319277,"title":"","content":"OK so to undermine my own post... I think I totally missed the point of several arguments that are being made. Also this post is almost stream of consciousness for me to try and work out some general thoughts of Promethean I have. So apologies beforehand for this possibly kinda being besides the point.<br /> <br /> It also kinda took a while to write, so I missed a few peoples updates that I think kinda make this a little redundant...oh well. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=319148#post319148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Whether demonizing transhumanism, or a certain variety of transhumanism, is the right decision thematically is another issue. I just definitely don't think it's an issue of transhumanists looking around, going &quot;that thing has positive stuff to say about the human condition! FUCK THAT!&quot; Instead they show up when the moral shifts away from &quot;humanity is neat&quot; to &quot;trying to be immortal (or transcend some other limitation) is wrong and always ends badly, always&quot;. Assuming their issue is with the former will probably lead to you misunderstanding them most of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though Arc has beat me to this point. I think it bears repeating:<br /> <br /> Considering the base assumption of the horror genre and the WoD is that getting involved and progressing is actually a worse state of affairs then leaving well alone the statement that:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;X if engaged with (almost) always ends badly and will/has negative consequences for you.&quot; </div> </div> </div>If we take this as a simple genre truth that is applied as a metaphysical truth for 9/10 situations in the WoD then the later argument you suggest Gabby is actually pretty damn valid. Because its <b>A FACT</b> of reality/the setting that its pretty much the case. This being said their are examples (I've detailed some in a previous post) that show their are exceptions to this rule. <br /> <br /> However, 9 times out of 10 its a bad idea. Its fun to tell a story about that 1 in 10 time, makes for an interesting game, but its the exception, not the rule. Its not something I think any WoD game should really support as a default assumption (as such an assumption would go against he default horror tone that all the games engage with to different degrees). Its fine for a sidebar somewhere in a core book and a reminder about the customization quality of the games, but it does not need to be a major emphasis and certainly not for Promethean (the most humanist of all the game lines). <br /> <br /> I think their is an additional wrinkle to the argument however. Namely, that their is the element of a &quot;quality of life&quot; so to speak. This is why humanism (which is progressive itself) is kinda &quot;safe&quot; even in the WoD. Humans can have pretty awesome lives and do pretty awesome things. Yes we get sick, are physically fragile, die eventually and are subject to all the nasty human evils we inflict on one another. However, overall people get to live their lives to a reasonable level of free-will, contentment and progression. Its only when the idea of having &quot;more&quot; then you need for these basic &quot;human&quot; quality of life e.g. Immortality that the idea I posit above and that Arc talked about previously in regards to the horror genre a bit kicks in. <br /> <br /> Prometheans have a terrible quality of life, easily the worst of any of the major splats of the NWoD (Changelings come close I guess) the point of their journey is to reach the point where they &quot;belong&quot; to the world in a native way. Hence why theirs no &quot;punishment&quot; for them trying to have &quot;more&quot; then there lot. <br /> <br /> On to the point about defining your own identity you brought up Gabby in response to Satchel's point.<br /> <br /> I think equating the Promethean condition and its drive towards a humanitarian (as opposed to a transhumanist/post-humanist/anti-humanist) end with something like a gender identity issue is not really a great comparison. I can see the parallels for sure (as sure that some of them are even purposefully engaged with), but I think equating the entirety of identity with gender is too narrow and simplistic a focus. <br /> <br /> Prometheans are constructing an identity wholesale, they try and create a human viewpoint that will facilitate their transformation into real human beings. Part (likely a huge part) of that is deciding a gender for sure, but there is more to it then that. If anything I'd say Prometheans have &quot;species dysmorphia&quot;. Not something we have in the real world obviously, but theoretically I see their problem as being the fish that wants to be, wish it was and feels a drive to be a bird, rather then a man feels he is truly a woman in the wrong body. <br /> <br /> So leading on from this is of course the argument of:<br /> <br /> &quot;Why can't the fish want to be a (insert animal X) instead of a bird?&quot; <br /> <br /> Well, that's when we get more into the in-game stuff that Promethean has involved with itself. <br /> <br /> The Divine Fire for reasons no one understand or knows considers humanity special. Prometheans being creature of the Divine Fire share this &quot;metaphysical bias&quot; as we might call it. Hence the innate drive towards the Pilgrimage and the New Dawn. Hence the Azothic Memories within them stoking them forward. I think of it like a sort of &quot;migration instinct&quot; you see in birds, its an innate, natural, instinctual and semi-conscious drive. Going back to the fact hat Prometheans form identity whole sale over their pilgrimage, this innate drive helps them and guides them towards that end. <br /> <br /> Of course Prometheans are free-willed beings, so they can reject that instinct decide they would rather be &quot;X instead of a bird&quot;, but that means actively going against their nature and denying the animating force they have in place of a soul. It would be the equivalent of a migrating bird staying in a climate that would result in its starvation.<br /> <br /> Given all this, I don't really see a reason why a Promethean could sustain a transhumanist viewpoint for very long. I get that they could and likely would come across the idea at some point on the Pilgrimage. Some of the braver ones might even try an embrace it. However, they would notice pretty quickly surely that they have stalled on the Pilgrimage and that something likely feels &quot;off&quot; or &quot;not right&quot;. I think some would turn back then, embrace what feels &quot;right&quot; or &quot;natural&quot; to them, if only because its a comfort to feel that you are progressing again. A few might hang on anyway, but stagnation is going to be the result, which leads to despair and Flux. Of course, the Hundred Handed are always waiting. <br /> <br /> Which is sorta a visions cycle isn't it? If the die hard transhumanist Prometheans end up as Centimani then it acts as a sort of social warning for later Prometheans to not dabble in that particular philosophy. Though I am sure many might still study transhumanism to understand humans and the &quot;flaws&quot; they see in themselves that Prometheans are likely just trying to understand as &quot;features&quot; of humanity. <br /> <br /> The second point to consider is consequence. I've already touched on possible consequences for a Promethean who &quot;abandons&quot; the New Dawn for a &quot;better ending&quot; but there is another point I'll bring up here. Deciding that you as a person are non-binary and don't fit into either gender but are unique is I imagine a difficult thing to work out and deal with. Society is largely gender binary in nature, so obviously deciding to not engage with the social construct of binary gender is going to have some social consequences (something you may be more experienced with then I give the tone of your previous post). <br /> <br /> For Prometheans the consequences of trying to &quot;not become human&quot; are pretty much all consuming. Even taking the fall to the Hundred Handed off the table that I talked about earlier, there is the simple fact that being a Promethean kinda sucks. Disquiet, Wasteland, Firestorms and activating Pandorans are the bread and butter of you existence. As you progress on the Pilgrimage these things are toned down a bit and you learn transmutations that can help with some of these aspects. Though its important to note that no matter how much supernatural power you emass you will never complete negate them. <br /> <br /> Prometheans who decide to &quot;reach for their own ending away from humanity&quot; or &quot;try to inform an identity removed from humanity&quot; (basically attempt not to be human but not be Promethean either) are going to continuously suffer from the consequences I mentioned above. They can cultivate the supernatural powers to take the edge of some of these, but its never going to mitigate them completely. Never really make it bearable. Never going to make them feel like the world does not hate them and reject them (and I do mean THE WORLD on a metaphysical level here, not just human social rejection). <br /> <br /> I can't imagine what's that like really, to know deep in yourself that metaphysically you &quot;don't belong&quot; (its ultimate rejection, beyond anything humans can actually experience) must do terrible things to a persons self. Hang in there all you want with your &quot;own definition&quot;, it never going to get better for you then what you have at that moment. Is it any wonder then that a Promethean would &quot;conform&quot; or &quot;compromise&quot; to being &quot;merely human&quot; if even that &quot;limited state&quot; promised relief and belonging from such feelings? I don't find it hard to imagine almost every person exposed to that capitulating to that drive in the face of such terrible suffering. <br /> <br /> As a final point:<br /> <br /> Yes I know this does not really address your issue with the fact that the game has a metaphysics that leads to all the details and ends I talked about above. Personally, I feel all of it is necessary to really sell the uniqueness of the game that is Promethean. I can see how it could be seen as limiting by some people. I can't say I could see it as hurtful or dangerous in its intent or message (then again I'm a white, upper middle class, heterosexual male so I'm about as &quot;target audience&quot; as you can get for the majority of societal norms anyway) However, I'll strongly stress that the games message is one to be taken within the context of the game and the NWoD as a whole and not necessarily a philosophical statement on how people should view humanity in the real world (not saying you can't differentiate between the two, just as a general statement). <br /> <br /> Anyway, I've rambled and this is post is very convoluted and I'm not sure it got the points across I wanted it too, but at least I tried. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T15:10:09-08:00","id":319399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=319129#post319129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the analogy to dysmorphia that I think you're implying is actually probably a big part of why this makes my personal and specific brain itch, so sure let's talk about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've implied no analogy. I've previously pointed at the developer's bringing up the phenomenon as a comparative experience to what the Created live with and amechra's just recently beaten at that particular drum, but my analogy of choice is and always has been the one where the Pilgrimage is the Promethean version of attempting to self-actualize their way out of existential-scale depression or at the very least out of the level of such where their entire universe reifies the sense that they are worthless and ought to expect destruction or ostracism. I have more experience with feeling like a useless sack of bad ideas than anything to do with the constellation of elements particular to dysmorphia and my view of the material is reflective of this.<br /> <br /> I find it unproductive to argue about Doylist standpoints on the fundamental basics of the gameline and the aforementioned disregarding of the Watsonian elements of the material feeds into my recurring annoyance at people's making arguments that rely on <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centipede_mathematics\" target=\"_blank\">centipede</a> structuralism. &quot;Becoming this one specific thing instead of something else&quot; presumes there is something else that one can reasonably become that possesses the qualities one is attempting to gain and retain \u2014 an assumption that doesn't bear out when the best fits for that either directly draw from that one specific thing or are the result of something becoming more like that one specific thing.<br /> <br /> The examples we have on the books of Prometheans becoming other things include, in the form of rumors:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Spirits - for which the keys to the process are specifically mentioned as a cautionary tale about the Ulgans.<br /> \u2022 Some kind of pure-Elpis &quot;Pyros-god&quot; - the direct skipping to immortality of which is specifically noted to have spawned a number of attempted imitators.<br /> \u2022 King of an extradimensional Disquiet-free Flux-free shadow-world - which is rather irrelevant to anyone who hopes to accomplish the basic goal of self-transformation to stay on Earth.<br /> \u2022 A superhuman being of the sort who inspired legends of god-blooded heroes - as part of the end of the Pilgrimage.<br /> \u2022 A tree - dream-talking or otherwise, it's a <i>tree</i>.<br /> <br /> Understandably the New Dawn is rather decidedly the Promethean equivalent of the Golden Road Ascension method among archmagi - it's proven to work and the people interested in crossing the final threshold of their journey are few and far-between enough that the most reliable method gets the most credibility given the proportion of them that actually &quot;win.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strange Alchemies p104, When did the Promethean first learn about the Pilgrimage?</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Prometheans hear about the Great Work from the moment they are able to understand the concept, or even before. Others hear about it only as they are about to undertake their independence from their creators. Still others only hear their creator talk of it occasionally, or to other people, and they are never given any context for what it means. Some hear absolutely nothing about the Pilgrimage from their creators, and have to discover its existence from other Prometheans. The circumstances under which the Promethean hears of it, and from whom he hears it, can set the tone for his Pilgrimage. Those who hear of it from a cruel creator may walk it with hesitation, while others may consider the Pilgrimage the thing that took their beloved creators from them.<br /> <br /> Other Prometheans simply find themselves on the Pilgrimage. For some, they\u2019ve somehow always known that their goal was to be come human; it simply took someone else putting it into words for them. Others seek to be near humans, to emulate them, but do not understand why they do these things. <b>The Pilgrimage is an innate part of the Promethean existence \u2014 the Divine Fire is transformative, and rare is the Promethean who is simply content as he is. Prometheans are all driven by the desire for change, to become something else, and <u>most of them find their role models in humanity.</u></b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T19:19:06-08:00","id":319555,"title":"","content":"You kids doing alright in here? <br /> <br /> Okay, what's this Watson vs. Doyle thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T19:37:35-08:00","id":319564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=319555#post319555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, what's this Watson vs. Doyle thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>You want the non-lit-crit-nerd version?<br /> <br /> On-set versus off-stage.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">okay okay cryptic phrasing is no good<br /> <br /> By way of example: The Watsonian answer to &quot;why does the protagonist of this manga wind up not having to fight two of the BBEG's four lieutenants?&quot; is &quot;because one of them is plotting to betray the BBEG and the other is having a crisis of faith about the rightness of his master's cause, both of which mean they let the protagonist pass without fighting them or they get offed for disloyalty.&quot; The Doylist answer is &quot;because the author's serialization didn't get renewed and there were only so many issues left to wrap everything up.&quot;<br /> <br /> Watsonian interpretation looks at things in the context of the established story and setting. Doylist interpretation looks at things in the context of the author's thematic and extratextual intent and circumstances.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T19:43:48-08:00","id":319567,"title":"","content":"So my Google-fu didn't serve me ill.<br /> <br /> Carry on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T20:59:06-08:00","id":319591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=319139#post319139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcane talking out of his ass and not completely on topic time again!<br /> <br /> You know, part of the thing that bothers me about the transhumanists having issues with a humanist game is that it seems counter-intuitive to some degrees. I mean, there are things I like about tanshumanism and find worthwhile if other problems can be worked out ahead of time, but I think there should be a core of humanism in there that needs to help guide the ethical and moral practice of transhumanism, and having issues with a game that helps foster that sense strikes me as being a little off. On a very poor comparison, it's like hiring Frank Trollman*(real name, honest, look him up) to develop the 2nd Edition of the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> *<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/holden.shearer/posts/698754346876944?comment_id=700170113402034&amp;notif_t=like\" target=\"_blank\">Holden Shearer gives a spliel of Frank's that kind of hits on what I'm getting at.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>As an aside, Trollman actually tried to do exactly that, in the form of something called After Sundown.<br /> <br /> This was long after he lost his touch with writing, and as far as I can tell from the reviews, it ain't good.<br /> <br /> It's a lot like Promethean <i>as a gameline </i>in fact. There's something beautiful there, something new, but it just can't be at peace with itself and it comes off as a mockery of something more complete.<br /> <br /> We will now return to the actual topic;<br /> <br /> Honestly, Centimani always came off as people who use transhuman philosophy as a shield. It's like the sidebar in the corebook says, they claim to be monsters to escape from being human, because to them, humanity means nothing but pain. Similarly, it's one of the more petty concerns of becoming more than human; to some people, losing humanity is just another benefit, because loss of humanity means loss of baggage. Mortality, grief, social shame, all of that. The thing is, if you're turning to transhumanism to do <i>that...</i>yeah, something tells me you're interested in the power fantasy and not the philosophy. Power fantasies are fine and all, but it's not a way to live. Not in the real world. <br /> <br /> In that, they kind of remind me of Eclipse Phase's Exhumans, people who have so radically altered themselves that they have become as extraterrestrials. Normally, they'd simply be oddballs, but the thing about Exhumans is that they're <i>always </i>hostile, despite presumably remembering being human. Something tells me there's more than just the willingness to experiment with new things, there...Something involving a great deal of anger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T22:43:09-08:00","id":319648,"title":"","content":"Fun fact: if you google for &quot;horror&quot; and &quot;transhumanism&quot;, you get Eclipse Phase. I was sort of irritated to learn this, because I was hoping for a more academic perspective. Nope. Just links to stuff about Eclipse Phase.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T01:35:57-08:00","id":319723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=319073#post319073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that humanity is the basis for so many things in the WoD makes perfect sense, being as they're some of the only sentient things on the planet, which is why the obligate focus on humanity doesn't really strain my suspension of disbelief in other lines.<br /> <br /> Promethean starts with something that is a *person* but isn't a *human*, which makes it nearly unique (until demon came along), and then posits that well, of course, the best thing they could do would be to turn into us.<br /> <br /> Which is a sentence that leaves me scratching my head. It's such a bizarre and arrogant assumption. It hits me the same as white people rolling up on a foreign shore and saying &quot;these poor people, they haven't even got a fiat economy or organized religion, how willl they ever be happy unless they become like us?&quot;<br /> <br /> And I mean, the standard argument is &quot;well, that's part of the buy-in&quot; which is why, the first time I brought this up, it was in the context of shrugging and rejecting the buy-in. This time, I'm just popping up to say there's nothing particularly transhuman about that, transhumanism is something else that involves humans transcending the limits of humanity. This would just be...things that were never human, deciding that it's possible to be a fully realized person without being human. And trying to find that sense of fulfillment and identity in a world that actively and violently rejects all other ways of being.<br /> <br /> I think that could be a good story, but it's not particularly transhuman, it's just also not one the line creators are interested in telling.</div> </div> </div> </div>A reading of Promethean that essentially amounts to &quot;the Created = foreign people/people lacking privilege&quot; is one that never sat right with me. I mean, the WoD absolutely has that sort of thing, but it's not Promethean.<br /> <br /> I prefer the Promethean = children analogy. The Created aren't foreigners trying to fit in, find a place in society, reject their roots, emulate good, white Americans; they're little kids trying to figure out what it means to be a person. Orphans, too, because it's not like most of the Created receive any sort of education or parental love other than from other children who're just as confused as they are - if they're lucky. If at all. <br /> <br /> In that context, the Pilgrimage of the Created is a journey to figure out how to grow up, become an adult person, with the assorted advantages and problems; responsibility et al.<br /> <br /> The central question of Promethean is &quot;what does it mean to be human?&quot;. With this being the World of Darkness and all, Promethean doesn't view humanity through rose coloured lenses - the setting doesn't shy away from shedding light on all the terrible little things people do. This is why refinements such as Cobalus or Stannum exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 11-23-2014, 04:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T08:03:04-08:00","id":319887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=319591#post319591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As an aside, Trollman actually tried to do exactly that, in the form of something called After Sundown.<br /> <br /> This was long after he lost his touch with writing, and as far as I can tell from the reviews, it ain't good.<br /> <br /> It's a lot like Promethean <i>as a gameline </i>in fact. There's something beautiful there, something new, but it just can't be at peace with itself and it comes off as a mockery of something more complete.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not know that, but I'm not surprised by it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-23-2014, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T10:15:18-08:00","id":326125,"title":"","content":"I'm honestly not so certain that transhumanism is completely opposed to humanism in the first place. Think about it: humans as we know them have evolved to be optimized for a lifestyle of hunting and gathering somewhere on the warm East African savanna, with large social groups compared to most animals. We evolved to utilize simple tools such as spears and making fire to make hunting slightly easier and to unlock more nutrients from food, and we evolved capacity for language for, well, we're not sure why, but probably to promote social bonding, better protect from threats and better coordinate when hunting. <br /> <br /> Nothing from what I just wrote says a goddamn thing about turning wolves into dogs, turning grasses into wheat and rice, or turning hunter-gatherer bands into farming communities. There's nothing up there about killing the furriest mammal you can find and turning its hide into a warm coat to protect yourself against the Siberian cold. It says nothing about the invention of writing, or about laws and armies, about metallurgy and sailing. And that's just some of the stuff that happened before the common era. As a final exercise, compare the creature described in my first paragraph with the first living thing to set foot on the Moon, on another world entirely! All of humanity's history has been about transcending human limitations through cunning and hard work, to the point where instead of throwing rocks at other animals, we're throwing bits of metal at other planets, and where someone from 3000 years ago can leave a message for someone in the present day. The fact is, a part of the human spirit, that thing that humanism reveres, is all about transhumanism. <br /> <br /> And why couldn't realizing that be a milestone for a Promethean of an appropriate refinement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2925-melange_thief","name":"Melange_Thief","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T10:33:38-08:00","id":326131,"title":"","content":"To the extent that that\u2019s true, <b>Mage</b> is <i>much</i> better geared to address such things than <b>Promethean</b> is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T11:44:00-08:00","id":326177,"title":"","content":"Probably so, although I'm not familiar with Mage (yet, 2nd ed sounds really damn cool though). I'm bringing it up less as a way of saying &quot;Promethean MUST deal with this&quot; and more as showing how humanism and transhumanism can play ball, just in case someone needs a way of getting a transhumanist to get into the humanism buy-in for the game. Plus, for a Promethean who goes (or is about to go) Centimanus out of a transhumanist motivation, this realization could be something that gets them back on the Pilgrimage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2925-melange_thief","name":"Melange_Thief","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T18:32:47-08:00","id":326503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Melange_Thief</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=326177#post326177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably so, although I'm not familiar with Mage (yet, 2nd ed sounds really damn cool though). I'm bringing it up less as a way of saying &quot;Promethean MUST deal with this&quot; and more as showing how humanism and transhumanism can play ball, just in case someone needs a way of getting a transhumanist to get into the humanism buy-in for the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>The trouble with this is that &quot;transhumanism&quot; gets cited by a fair few people as a defense for &quot;becoming a human is lame&quot; as an argument rather than as any kind of support for actual transhumanism.<br /> <br /> Of all the lines, there's three whose supernatural abilities aren't associated with some degree of anachronism, creative sterility, or inability to sympathize with others, and of those, one involves literally altering the symbolism of the world through the awakened power of the human soul, and the other two (this game included) involve a being which may or may not be capital-G God in their metaphysics and definitely involve beings who are &quot;broken&quot; in contrast with beings that lack or forsake free will alongside empathy, creativity, learning, and the ability to change oneself under one's own power.<br /> <br /> One does not gain those things by emulating the latter and it does well to note that these qualities are not universally-possessed traits of sapient beings in the World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T10:35:54-08:00","id":327168,"title":"","content":"Promethean can be a transhumanist game if you look at it not as the beginning and end of the journey but as a first step towards a longer pilgrimage which culminates in becoming something more than human.<br /> First in <b>Promethean: The created</b> you start as something undefined, even antagonist to the universe. A mistake, a freak, something unwanted that has no identity or place in the world and therefore is rejected by everything. Then you start looking for definition and meaning in the world around you, in your search you come across the most fascinating and terrifying creature in the world, Humanity. Humans, such a wonderful and amazing creatures, what is that makes them so incredible? what is that makes so dynamic, so fascinating, so unique? How come a being so mercurial can find definition and meaning in the world? the answer is: potentiality. Humanity has the potential to be anything they want, to define themselves into whatever they desire. Whether or not they live up to that potential is not the point, the fact that they have the potential is the point. Seeing this fact how could the promethean not wish to be a creature with so many possibilities?. Before they can become something more they have to become SOMETHING, being human is the first step to become something that can be so much more. Having reached the end of their pilgrimage they become human, finishing their firs part of their journey towards transhumanity.<br /> Next we jump to the life of the new human in <b>Hunter: The vigil</b>. The Promethean at first enjoys his new found humanity, exploring it and trying find an even deeper meaning in it. However after a while he starts to wonder is there something more? He knows that there are many mysteries in the world that humanity is oblivious to. Also all kinds of creatures at the shores of civilization and human society. Hell till recently he was one of those things, so who better to take the vigil and stand up for their new family than an ex promethean? Armed with his knowledge and his love for humans he takes the torch of the vigil and walks into the darkness. It's important to understand that the vigil is not just about hunting or protecting, it can be just that but that's a very limited way to see it. It can also about learning and understanding a world that has a lot more going on that it shows. In the process of following the vigil the ex-promethean learns more about the occult secrets of the world and how they interact with humanity. Bit by bit they gather more knowledge and become wiser, understanding the complexities of the world and it's many layers. Then, if the vigil hasn't taken their life there comes a moment, an epiphany that shakes them to their very core. The illuminating moment that comes after years of growth in which their souls becomes exalted and they awaken.<br /> Finally we arrive to <b>Mage: The awakening </b>in which the ex-promethean becomes a mage. All that effort, all that work, all the pain and suffering, culminates in the awakening of their soul and becoming something far more that human. They are no longer constrained to define themselves and reality in small ways, now they can meddle with the higher definitions and concepts themselves. They have pulled away the veil and stared at the source of the universe and in the process they gained a bigger perspective of reality. Nevertheless becoming a mage is not the end of the road, it's just the final step in his pilgrimage. There's still a lot of growth to do and learn from their new condition. Using everything that he has learned form his journey he can start his road to ascension. He started being nothing and has arrived to the point that he can decided what is and isn't. Becoming transhuman doesn't mean becoming something inhuman. It's breaking the chains that limit humans and become more, much more. Walking this road to the end allows them to truly become transhuman.<br /> <br /> I hope you liked my explanation, one day I would like to run a chronicle like this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 12-01-2014, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T10:51:51-08:00","id":327182,"title":"","content":"So, what you're saying is...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Peace is a lie, there is only passion.<br /> Through passion, I gain strength.<br /> Through strength, I gain power.<br /> Through power, I gain victory.<br /> Through victory, my chains are broken.<br /> The Force shall free me. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T11:31:03-08:00","id":327218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=327182#post327182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what you're saying is...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It is one road among many, you could see the road to transhumanism as the ultimate freedom. Freedom from weakness and being defined by the universe, instead YOU define the universe. However as I said before it's just one way, everyone has to find their own path. The point is you make your own path. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 12-01-2014, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T11:55:10-08:00","id":327269,"title":"","content":"That's all well and good Firanai but its well outside the scope of Promethean as a game. <br /> <br /> As you point out yourself, you need to involve Vigil and Awakening to actually bridge the thematic gap into transhuman themes and make it work. If you want to bring in other games lines that's fine, but it has little to do with Promethean as its own game in the NWoD.<br /> <br /> Also you second step into the Vigil does make a bit of presumption that the ex-Promethean remembers being a Promethean, something that in 1E (we don't know about 2E yet) was simply not the case. <br /> <br /> The general point that Transhuman themes are an ill match for Promethean basically stands as it always has. Within the humanist perspective of Promethean trying to be &quot;more then human&quot; leads a person (alchemists are a good example of humans attempts, I'm not just limiting this to Prometheans) to inhumanity, rather then any sort of transcendence to something better. <br /> <br /> Which, considering that within the scope of Promethean humans are special and the game is about fundamentally humanist themes tonally makes sense and pretty much is as it should be thematically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T12:40:25-08:00","id":327313,"title":"","content":"I agree with you, it was just a suggestion if you want to create a transhumanist chronicle with promethean as a base. By itself the game is about humanism and thats fine by me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T23:36:09-08:00","id":327926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=327218#post327218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is one road among many, you could see the road to transhumanism as the ultimate freedom. Freedom from weakness and being defined by the universe, instead YOU define the universe. However as I said before it's just one way, everyone has to find their own path. The point is you make your own path. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can't decide whether or not you realized I was quoting the Sith Code.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mys